Title: Quadratic differentials in Teichm\"uller theory and complex harmonic
  maps
Authors: Christian El Emam, Nathaniel Sagman
Categories: math.DG math.GT
\\
  We show that Hitchin-Wolf's harmonic map parametrization of Teichm\"uller
space, the Schwarzian holonomy map, and Uhlenbeck's almost-Fuchsian holonomy
map all arise as restrictions of a single locally biholomorphic map into the
$\mathrm{PSL}(2,\mathbb{C})$ character variety. The map admits a right inverse
defined on an open subset of quasi-Fuchsian space, encoding harmonic maps
together with the Bers embedding. The construction goes through complex
harmonic maps to the space of oriented geodesics of $\mathbb{H}^3$.
  Along the way, we further develop the theory of complex harmonic maps, with a
focus on the natural $\mathbb{C}^*$-action and the relation to complex
projective structures. This leads to an independent application: we obtain a
new geometric interpretation of certain real twistor lines in the rank-two
Deligne-Hitchin moduli space and we recover a theorem of Gothen-Silva.
